meta {
  name: Download a fortnight as it will actually fall
  type: http
  seq: 81
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-export.xlsx?branch_id={{branchId}}&mode=range&from=2026-11-02&to=2026-11-09
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.headers['content-type']: eq application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet
}

docs {
  A different document from the pattern above. Columns are dates, not weekdays,
  and every cell has been through the occurrence resolver: holidays are marked
  and their periods are not left blank, cancellations and substitutions are
  named, a retimed lesson carries its own clock span, and a day that substitutes
  another weekday runs that weekday's lessons with "runs as Monday" in its
  header.

  It is perishable by construction - it is wrong the moment a deviation is
  recorded after it was downloaded - so it is the option and the pattern is the
  default.

  The range is capped at 62 days. Four hundred columns is not a document
  anybody reads.
}
